This repo is used to store my configuration files on Linux (and macOS).

Dotfiles are managed with chezmoi (https://www.chezmoi.io/).

Layout
------
  .chezmoiroot          tells chezmoi the source state lives in home/
  home/                 chezmoi source state (mirrors $HOME)
    dot_bashrc            -> ~/.bashrc  (dot_ = leading ".")
    create_dot_bash_exports -> ~/.bash_exports, only created if missing
                             (put machine-local exports/secrets here)
    modify_dot_gitconfig.tmpl -> ~/.gitconfig, merged via update_gitconfig.py
                             so the machine's [user]/[credential] sections stay
    dot_config/nvim/      -> ~/.config/nvim/init.vim (= .vimrc; only if nvim exists)
    dot_config/kitty/     -> ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf (only if kitty exists)
    dot_local/bin/        -> ~/.local/bin (runwlog, ...)
    .chezmoiscripts/      one-off setup scripts (bracketed-paste fix)
  .gitconfig            base git config consumed by update_gitconfig.py
  install_*.sh, etc.    standalone tool installers, not managed by chezmoi

First-time setup
----------------
  git clone <this repo> ~/projects/dotfiles
  ~/projects/dotfiles/setup_dot.sh     # installs chezmoi if needed, then applies

Day to day
----------
  chezmoi diff                 # preview what would change in $HOME
  chezmoi apply                # apply the repo to $HOME
  chezmoi edit --apply ~/.bashrc
  chezmoi re-add ~/.bashrc     # pull edits made directly in $HOME back into the repo
  chezmoi cd                   # open a shell in this repo
